.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt NOVI-HWDETECT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm novi-hwdetect
.Nd load drivers for the hardware in this machine
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
walks
.Pa /sys/devices/**/modalias
and hands each string to
modprobe(8),
which matches it against the
.Pa modules.alias
that
depmod(8)
generated at build time.
That is udev's builtin driver loader in fifteen lines, and it is the
.Em only
generic one on this system: every other module load here is a
hardcoded list, and all three of them were written against QEMU.
.Pp
It runs
.Sy in the initramfs, before the root search .
That placement is the point: a storage controller nobody listed
otherwise ends in an emergency shell.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/lib/modules/*/modules.alias" -compact
.It Pa /sys/devices
Walked for
.Pa modalias
files.
.It Pa /lib/modules/ Ns Ar version Ns Pa /modules.alias
The table
modprobe(8)
matches against.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
It exits 0 when a module fails to load: a driver that is absent is
not a reason to stop booting.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-hotplug 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0011.
.Sh CAVEATS
.Nm
is
.Sy coldplug
and cannot be anything else.
It walks
.Pa /sys
once, so it answers
.Dq what is in this machine
and never
.Dq what did someone just plug in .
.Xr novi-hotplug 8
is the same rule driven by the kernel's uevent stream.
Two sources, one rule: do not merge them, and do not let either grow
a device list.
.Pp
A script that runs in the initramfs may use only the busybox applets
.Nm mkinitramfs.sh
links, and that list is hand-written.
.Nm
once loaded every driver correctly and then died on
.Dq tr: not found .
.Pp
None of this has run on physical hardware.
It is verified on three virtio devices, which is the easiest case
there is.
